  "body": "Part of #308. Depends on #317 (carried body).\n\n## Proposal\n- Fixture collision (M3.2 B fixtures) checks tool and holder against the carried stock plus that setup's fixtures (a re-clamped part held on a face setup 1 machined).\n- Lathe / mill-turn second operation (part flip or sub-spindle hand-off): decide whether it uses the same carried-body mechanism (transform = flip about the spindle normal + Z shift) or the turning field, implement it, and refuse the rest by name.\n- Performance: cache the carried body per setup keyed by the upstream digests and the transform; re-sample only on change; measure on the big fixtures (heavy lane).\n\n## Done means\nFixture collisions read the carried stock (pinned); the lathe second-op path is implemented or refused by name; the carried body is not recomputed on an unrelated edit (pinned by a counter).\n",
